def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(184, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND IF THE LORD YOUR GOD ENLARGES YOUR BORDER" (19:8) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE MATTER, FOR ITS REWARD HE WILL ENLARGE YOUR BORDER. ({SP_(184, 1, "עשה", "מצוה", "האמורה", "בענין")} "do the commandment stated in the matter"; {SP_(184, 1, "שבשכרה", "ירחיב")} "for whose reward He will enlarge"): THE CONDITION\'S ARMS — 19:8-9\'s "if … when you keep" read as reward: the three more cities a CONDITIONAL on the border\'s enlargement (12:20\'s twin) — the compile\'s condition (the readback\'s question: never fired on the tape). Fresh.')
srow(184, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"AS HE SWORE TO YOUR FATHERS" — ALL BY THE MERIT OF YOUR FATHERS. ({SP_(184, 2, "הכל", "בזכות", "אבותיך")} "all by the merit of your fathers"): the oath\'s ground the fathers\' merit (179:1\'s "by your merit" beside it) — an aggadic gloss, no rule. Fresh.')
srow(184, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND GIVES YOU ALL THE LAND" — ALL BY THE MERIT OF YOUR FATHERS. ({SP_(184, 3, "הכל", "בזכות", "אבותיך")} "all by the merit of your fathers"): the same gloss on the second clause. Fresh.')
srow(185, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU KEEP ALL THIS COMMANDMENT … YOU SHALL ADD THREE MORE CITIES TO THESE THREE" (19:9) — FROM HERE: MOSES SEPARATED THREE BEYOND THE JORDAN; WHEN THEY CAME TO THE LAND THEY SEPARATED THREE MORE; IN THE FUTURE THEY WILL SEPARATE THREE MORE — THREE ON THREE ARE SIX, AND THREE MORE, NINE. ({SP_(185, 1, "שלש", "ערים", "הפריש", "משה", "בעבר", "הירדן")} "three cities Moses separated beyond the Jordan"; {SP_(185, 1, "ועוד", "שלש", "הרי", "תשע")} "and three more — nine"): THE COUNT OF THE CITIES 3 + 3 + 3 = 9 (Makkot 2:4 the English\'s note; 4:41-43 and Joshua 20 the tape\'s three and three, the third three the future\'s) — the compile\'s parameter with the future arm untriggered. Fresh.')
srow(185, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'R. NEHORAI: THREE ON THREE, AND MORE — NINE; "ON THE THREE" — TWELVE. ({SP_(185, 2, "הרי", "שתים", "עשרה")} "twelve"): the count read from the verse\'s doubled "three" — a DISPUTE on the parameter (9 / 12 / 15). Fresh.')
srow(185, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'R. SAUL: THREE ON THREE, AND MORE — NINE; ON THE THREE — TWELVE; "THESE" — FIFTEEN. ({SP_(185, 3, "האלה", "הרי", "חמש", "עשרה")} "these — fifteen"): the third reading; the compile keeps the dispute as data (the answer sheet Makkot 2:4 says nine — the Sifrei\'s own first row). Fresh.')
srow(186, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT INNOCENT BLOOD BE NOT SHED … AND BLOOD BE UPON YOU" (19:10) — TO WARN THE COURT ABOUT THIS. ({SP_(186, 1, "להזהיר", "בית", "דין", "על", "כך")} "to warn the court about this"): the innocent blood a charge on the COURT (the cities unseparated = the court\'s blood-guilt; Makkot 10a, not opened) — 183:8\'s form; the compile\'s effect "blood upon you" written on the court, not the killer. Fresh.')
srow(186, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHEN A MAN HATES HIS NEIGHBOR AND LIES IN WAIT AND RISES AGAINST HIM" (19:11) — FROM HERE THEY SAID: ONE WHO TRANSGRESSES A LIGHT COMMANDMENT WILL END TRANSGRESSING A WEIGHTY ONE — "LOVE YOUR NEIGHBOR", "DO NOT TAKE VENGEANCE OR BEAR A GRUDGE", "DO NOT HATE YOUR BROTHER", "THAT YOUR BROTHER MAY LIVE WITH YOU" — UNTIL HE COMES TO BLOODSHED. ({SP_(186, 2, "עבר", "אדם", "על", "מצוה", "קלה")} "a man transgressed a light commandment"; {SP_(186, 2, "לידי", "שפיכות", "דמים")} "to bloodshed"): THE LADDER OF HATRED (Leviticus 19:17-18, 25:36 cited) — the moral reading of the intentional killer\'s verse; no rule for the compile (the hatred is the parameter, its history not). Fresh.')
srow(187, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'FROM HERE R. YOSE B. R. JUDAH: ONE WHO KILLS, UNWITTINGLY OR INTENTIONALLY — ALL RUN FIRST TO THE CITIES OF REFUGE; THE COURT SENDS AND BRINGS THEM FROM THERE. The headless piska\'s first row ({SP_(187, 1, "בין", "בשוגג", "בין", "במזיד")} "whether unwitting or intentional"; {SP_(187, 1, "הכל", "מקדימים", "לערי", "מקלט")} "all go first to the cities of refuge"): THE PROCEDURE — every killer flees first, the court fetches (Makkot 2:6 the English\'s note, the Sifrei dropping "originally") — the compile\'s two-stage state (fled; tried). Fresh.')
srow(187, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE LIABLE TO DEATH — THEY KILLED HIM, AS IT SAYS "THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY SEND AND TAKE HIM FROM THERE" (19:12). ({SP_(187, 2, "מי", "שנתחיב", "מיתה", "הרגוהו")} "one liable to death — they killed him"): the intentional killer\'s arm — the elders extradite, the avenger kills. Fresh.')
srow(187, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE NOT LIABLE TO DEATH — THEY RELEASED HIM, AS IT SAYS "THE CONGREGATION SHALL DELIVER THE MANSLAYER" (NUMBERS 35:25). ({SP_(187, 3, "מי", "שלא", "נתחיב", "מיתה", "פטרוהו")} "one not liable to death — they released him"): the acquitted arm — Numbers 35:25 read into Deuteronomy\'s procedure (the refuge runner\'s cell called). Fresh.')
srow(187, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'ONE LIABLE TO EXILE — THEY RETURN HIM TO HIS PLACE, AS IT SAYS "THE CONGREGATION SHALL RESTORE HIM" (NUMBERS 35:25). ({SP_(187, 4, "מי", "שנתחיב", "גלות", "מחזירים", "אותו", "למקומו")} "one liable to exile — they return him to his place"): the third arm — the unwitting killer sent back to the city (Makkot 2:6): THE THREE VERDICTS of the court on a fled killer (death / free / exile) — the compile\'s cell. Fresh.')
srow(187, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'RABBI: A MANSLAYER WHO WENT TO A CITY OF REFUGE THINKING IT RECEIVES HIM AS IT RECEIVES THE UNWITTING — THE ELDERS OF THE CITY SEND AND BRING HIM FROM THERE, "THE ELDERS OF HIS CITY SHALL SEND". ({SP_(187, 5, "כסבור", "שקולטתו")} "thinking it receives him"; {SP_(187, 5, "זקני", "העיר", "שולחים")} "the elders of the city send"): Rabbi\'s reading — the intentional killer who fled in error is fetched (the same procedure by another door); "his city" the killer\'s home city\'s elders (Makkot 10b, not opened). Fresh.')
srow(187, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND HE DIES BY THE AVENGER\'S HAND" — WHENCE, IF HE DID NOT DIE BY THE AVENGER\'S HAND, HE DIES BY ANY MAN\'S HAND? THE TEACHING SAYS 19:12-13 "GIVE HIM INTO THE AVENGER\'S HAND AND HE DIES; YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY". ({SP_(187, 6, "ימות", "ביד", "כל", "אדם")} "he dies by any man\'s hand"): THE EXECUTOR WIDENED — the avenger first, any man after (Makkot 2:7 the English\'s note; 17:7\'s "the witnesses\' hand first" the form) — the compile\'s executor parameter. Fresh.')
srow(187, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'LEST YOU SAY: SINCE THIS ONE WAS KILLED, WHY SHOULD WE BE LIABLE FOR THIS ONE\'S BLOOD? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY HIM, AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE INNOCENT BLOOD" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(187, 7, "למה", "אנו", "באים", "לחוב", "בדמו")} "why should we come to be liable for his blood"; {SP_(187, 7, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): THE PURGE FORMULA\'S THIRD FORM ("purge the innocent blood", 19:13 — once in the Bible) read as PERSONS, "the doers of evil" — the same reading the Sifrei gives 13:6 and 17:7 (the seducers\' and the idolater\'s), and Onkelos writes it (19:13 "remove the shedders"): the effect\'s name evil_purged at its seat. Fresh.')
srow(188, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT MOVE YOUR NEIGHBOR\'S LANDMARK" (19:14) — WAS IT NOT ALREADY SAID "YOU SHALL NOT ROB" (LEVITICUS 19:13)? WHY "YOU SHALL NOT MOVE"? WHOEVER UPROOTS HIS FELLOW\'S BOUNDARY TRANSGRESSES TWO PROHIBITIONS. ({SP_(188, 1, "עובר", "בשני", "לאוים")} "transgresses two prohibitions"): THE LANDMARK A SECOND PROHIBITION over robbery — the compile\'s effect a doubled transgression (the count of prohibitions the answer). Fresh.')
srow(188, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT APPLY OUTSIDE THE LAND? THE TEACHING SAYS "IN YOUR INHERITANCE WHICH YOU INHERIT" — IN THE LAND OF ISRAEL TWO PROHIBITIONS, OUTSIDE THE LAND ONLY ONE. ({SP_(188, 2, "בחוצה", "לארץ", "אינו", "עובר", "אלא", "משום", "לאו", "אחד")} "outside the land he transgresses only one prohibition"): the landmark\'s law LAND-BOUND, robbery everywhere — the compile\'s place parameter (in the land: two; outside: one). Fresh.')
srow(188, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WHO UPROOTS THE TRIBES\' BOUNDARIES TRANSGRESSES? "YOU SHALL NOT MOVE YOUR NEIGHBOR\'S LANDMARK". WHENCE ONE WHO EXCHANGES R. ELIEZER\'S WORDS FOR R. JOSHUA\'S, AND SAYS OF THE UNCLEAN CLEAN AND OF THE CLEAN UNCLEAN? THE SAME. WHENCE ONE WHO SELLS HIS FATHERS\' GRAVE? THE SAME — MIGHT IT BE EVEN IF NO ONE WAS EVER BURIED IN IT? "IN YOUR INHERITANCE WHICH YOU INHERIT" — IF EVEN ONE STILLBORN WAS BURIED THERE WITH PERMISSION, HE TRANSGRESSES. ({SP_(188, 3, "תחומים", "של", "שבטים")} "the tribes\' boundaries"; {SP_(188, 3, "למחליף", "דברי", "רבי", "אליעזר")} "one who exchanges R. Eliezer\'s words"; {SP_(188, 3, "למוכר", "קבר", "אבותיו")} "one who sells his fathers\' grave"; {SP_(188, 3, "אפלו", "נפל", "אחד")} "even one stillborn"): THE LANDMARK WIDENED THREE WAYS — the tribal bounds, the TRADITIONS\' ATTRIBUTIONS (the teachers\' names as boundaries — the reading\'s own law of the ledger), the ancestral tomb (the stillborn\'s burial the threshold) — the compile keeps the three as effects\' seats with the tomb\'s parameter. Fresh.')
srow(188, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"ONE WITNESS SHALL NOT RISE AGAINST A MAN" (19:15) — I HAVE ONLY CAPITAL CASES; MONETARY CASES? THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR ANY INIQUITY". ({SP_(188, 4, "לדיני", "ממונות", "מנין")} "monetary cases — whence?"; {SP_(188, 4, "לכל", "עון")} "for any iniquity"): the two-witness rule extended to MONEY by "any iniquity" — the compile\'s evidence parameter over both case classes (17:6\'s twin at capital cases). Fresh.')
srow(188, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'OFFERINGS? "AND FOR ANY SIN (CHATAT)". ({SP_(188, 5, "לקרבנות", "מנין")} "offerings — whence?"): the sin-offering\'s liability needs two witnesses (Keritot 3:1 the English\'s note — one witness against his own denial): the third class — the row with no verse citation in either file (the ink\'s seventeen). Fresh.')
srow(188, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'LASHES? "IN ANY SIN WHICH HE SINS". ({SP_(188, 6, "למכות", "מנין")} "lashes — whence?"): the fourth class — the three words "iniquity, sin, transgression" the three case classes beside the capital: the compile\'s witness count applies to every verdict kind. Fresh.')
srow(188, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'TO RAISE TO THE PRIESTHOOD OR LOWER FROM IT? "FOR ANY INIQUITY AND FOR ANY SIN". ({SP_(188, 7, "להעלות", "לכהונה", "ולהוריד", "מן", "הכהונה")} "to raise to the priesthood and to lower from the priesthood"): the LINEAGE STATUS needs two witnesses — the compile\'s status writes (priest / not) under the same evidence rule. Fresh.')
srow(188, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'I HAVE ONLY TESTIMONY AGAINST A MAN; A WOMAN? "FOR ANY INIQUITY … WHICH HE SINS". IF WE INCLUDE THE WOMAN, WHY "AGAINST A MAN"? FOR INIQUITY HE STANDS NOT, BUT HE STANDS AGAINST A WOMAN TO MARRY HER — R. JUDAH. ({SP_(188, 8, "לעדות", "אשה", "מנין")} "testimony against a woman — whence?"; {SP_(188, 8, "קם", "הוא", "באשה", "להשיאה")} "he stands against a woman to marry her"): ONE WITNESS SUFFICES to free a woman to remarry (Yevamot 16:7 the English\'s note — the husband\'s death by one witness): the compile\'s one-witness exception (marriage status). Fresh.')
srow(188, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE: FOR INIQUITY HE STANDS NOT, BUT HE STANDS FOR AN OATH. R. YOSE\'S ARGUMENT: WHERE HIS OWN MOUTH DOES NOT JOIN ONE WITNESS FOR DEATH, HE SWEARS BY HIS OWN MOUTH; WHERE HIS MOUTH JOINS ONE WITNESS FOR MONEY, SHOULD HE NOT SWEAR? NO — ONE WHO SWEARS BY HIS OWN MOUTH PAYS BY HIS OWN MOUTH; SHALL HE SWEAR BY ONE WITNESS WHEN HE DOES NOT PAY BY ONE WITNESS? THE TEACHING SAYS "FOR ANY INIQUITY" — FOR INIQUITY HE STANDS NOT, HE STANDS FOR AN OATH. ({SP_(188, 9, "קם", "הוא", "לשבועה")} "he stands for an oath"; {SP_(188, 9, "קל", "וחמר", "הדברים")} "the matter is an a-fortiori"): ONE WITNESS IMPOSES AN OATH (Shevuot 5:4-6 the English\'s notes — the a-fortiori proposed and refuted, the verse decides) — the compile\'s second one-witness effect (oath_imposed). Fresh.')
srow(188, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"BY THE MOUTH OF TWO WITNESSES OR BY THE MOUTH OF THREE WITNESSES A MATTER STANDS" — NOT BY THEIR WRITING, NOR BY THE MOUTH OF AN INTERPRETER. ({SP_(188, 10, "לא", "על", "פי", "כתבם")} "not by their writing"; {SP_(188, 10, "ולא", "על", "פי", "תורגמן")} "and not by an interpreter"): "BY THE MOUTH" LITERAL — oral testimony, no document, no interpreter (Makkot 1:9 the English\'s note) — the compile\'s testimony-form parameter. Fresh.')
srow(188, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'"BY THE MOUTH OF TWO" — FROM HERE THEY SAID: THE HUSBAND WHO WARNS HIS WIFE — R. ELIEZER: WARNS BY TWO AND MAKES HER DRINK BY ONE. FOR IT WOULD STAND TO REASON: THE FIRST TESTIMONY, WHICH DOES NOT FORBID HER FOREVER, NEEDS TWO — THE LAST, WHICH FORBIDS HER FOREVER, SURELY? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND THERE IS NO WITNESS AGAINST HER" (NUMBERS 5:13) — ANY WITNESS AGAINST HER, SHE DOES NOT DRINK. ({SP_(188, 11, "מקנא", "על", "פי", "שנים")} "he warns by two"; {SP_(188, 11, "ומשקה", "על", "פי", "עד", "אחד")} "and makes her drink by one witness"): THE SOTAH\'S TWO COUNTS (Sotah 1:1 and 6:3 the English\'s notes) hung on 19:15\'s "two" — the sotah runner\'s parameters cited by the witnesses\' law (the a-fortiori refuted by Numbers 5:13). Fresh.')
